  "details": "More specifically, I'm talking about when you're in an instance with someone you have a blocking situation with, and you view their profile in the quick menu.\n\nHowever, this should also apply to any of these features that are available by viewing profiles directly through user search, whether through the client or the website, too (like gifting VRC+).\n\nThis should not be the case. If you have blocked someone, or they have blocked you, all options other than \"unblock user\" and \"vote to kick\" should be disabled and hidden (and you should be able to vote kick people you have blocked, currently this is not the case afaik - if you don't plan to do that then I guess you should just hide this button too). Unless they're an instance owner or moderator, in which case obviously you should still have your instance moderator toolkit.\n\nI've personally known people who have been harassed by being gifted VRC+ by people who they have blocked, that option should most definitely not exist under these circumstances. Assuming \"invite to group\" works, that shouldn't either. The rest are more benign, but really none of those functions should work or be displayed anymore when dealing with blocked users.\n\nI'm filing this as a bug report because I assume the current behavior is an oversight and isn't intentional. If it is, sort it under feature requests then.\n\nThanks.",
